<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104526" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τράμις</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span> (not found in gen. sg.),
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the perineum</i> or <i>line which divides the scrotum and
				runs on to the breech,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				195
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hippon.
				84
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				246
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
				<u>Onom.</u>
				101
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Lex.</u>
				2
			</span></i>:—the acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τράμιν</span>
			has a long <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ι,</span> if <i><span class="en">
				Hippon.
			</span></i> l.c. is sound; the acc. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τράμην</span></b>  in <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				763.56
			</span></i> is 
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τράμιν</span>
			, cf. Sch.Luc.<i><span class="en">
				p.191
			</span></i> R.</div>
